<!--
  Junction page § Service. Facts: packages/junction/README.md (Litestone ORM:
  createService generates find/get/create/patch/remove, validation from the
  schema, paginate { default, max }, methods: narrows the surface and the spec;
  OpenAPI), AGENTS.md (the one rule: the schema grades the caller, the file
  name is the service name), test/openapi-round-trip.test.ts (every operation
  the spec documents is one the wire answers, 14 pass on 2026-11-03).
  The proof is a real run: a scratch app over packages/junction and
  packages/litestone (db/schema.lite 8 lines, services/tasks.service.ts 3
  lines, a stub auth for sign-in), driven with curl on 2026-11-03. Responses
  are abridged where marked.
  Not claimed: that the OpenAPI document carries the model's field schemas.
  Without a declared schemas: entry or input: type, the request body of a
  create is not in the spec (probed: the POST operation has no requestBody).
-->
<script>
  const CODE = `// db/schema.lite
model Task {
  id        Int      @id
  title     String   @length(1, 80) @trim
  done      Boolean  @default(false)
  createdAt DateTime @default(now())

  @@gate(0.4.4.5)   // read: anyone · create, update: signed in · delete: level 5
}

// api/src/services/tasks.service.ts
import { createService } from '@frontierjs/junction'

export default createService({ paginate: { default: 3, max: 50 } })`

  const RUN = `POST /api/tasks  {"title":"  Ship the docs  "}      (signed in)
  201  {"id":1,"title":"Ship the docs","done":false,"createdAt":"…"}
POST /api/tasks  {"title":""}
  400  {"message":"title: title must be at least 1 character",
        "data":[{"field":"title", …}]}
POST /api/tasks  {"title":"anon"}                          (no token)
  401  {"message":"Authentication required"}
DELETE /api/tasks/1                                        (signed in)
  403  {"message":"\\"Task.delete\\" requires level 5, user has level 4"}

GET /api/tasks
  200  {"data":[{"id":1, …},{"id":2, …},{"id":3, …}],
        "total":6,"limit":3,"offset":0,"hasMore":true,"endCursor":"…"}
GET /api/tasks?$limit=2&$offset=1&$orderBy=-id
  200  {"data":[{"id":5, …},{"id":4, …}],
        "total":6,"limit":2,"offset":1,"hasMore":true}
GET /api/tasks?$limit=500
  400  {"message":"$limit 500 is above this service's maximum page of 50. …"}
GET /api/tasks?nope=1
  400  {"message":"Unknown filter key 'nope' — did you mean 'done'?. Filterable
        fields on Task: createdAt, done, id, title. …"}

GET /api/openapi.json
  openapi 3.1.0
  /api/tasks        get, post
  /api/tasks/{id}   get, patch, delete`
</script>

<section id="service" class="bc-section">
  <div class="container stack">
    <p class="eyebrow">A service from a model</p>
    <h2>The CRUD, the checks and the paging are already written.</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      A service file over a Litestone model answers find, get, create, patch and remove, and
      grades every call by the model's own rules. You write only what the model cannot say.
    </p>

    <div class="bc-split">
      <ul class="bc-points">
        <li>
          <strong>The file name picks the model.</strong>
          <code>tasks.service.ts</code> is the service <code>tasks</code> over <code>Task</code>,
          autoloaded, and the OpenAPI document lists exactly what it answers, so narrowing
          <code>methods:</code> narrows the spec too.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Validation is the field's own rules.</strong>
          <code>@length(1, 80) @trim</code> is the 400 on create, and a filter on a column that
          does not exist is refused by name instead of ignored.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Authorization is the gate, not a hook.</strong>
          <code>@@gate</code> answers 401 to a stranger and 403 to a caller a level short, in
          the schema where every other path meets it too.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>A page has a ceiling.</strong>
          <code>paginate: &#123; default, max &#125;</code> sets the size, the answer carries
          <code>total</code> and <code>hasMore</code>, and a request over the max is refused
          with the number it may ask for.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <figure class="bc-proof">
        <pre class="code">{CODE}</pre>
        <pre class="code">{RUN}</pre>
        <figcaption>
          A scratch app on this repo's Junction and Litestone, run with curl on 2026-11-03: the
          schema and the 3-line service file above (import path shortened to the package name),
          with a stub auth for sign-in and the OpenAPI plugin around it. Responses are abridged,
          cut to the status and the lines that matter, and <code>…</code> marks what was cut.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <p class="bc-more">
      Read more:
      <a href="https://github.com/frontierjs/frontierjs/blob/main/packages/junction/README.md#litestone-orm">createService over a Litestone model</a> ·
      <a href="https://github.com/frontierjs/frontierjs/blob/main/packages/junction/README.md#methods--the-surface-declared">narrowing the surface with methods</a> ·
      <a href="https://github.com/frontierjs/frontierjs/blob/main/packages/junction/README.md#openapi">OpenAPI</a> ·
      <a href="https://github.com/frontierjs/frontierjs/blob/main/packages/junction/AGENTS.md">the schema grades the caller</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .bc-proof pre.code { overflow-x: auto; font-size: .82rem; }
  .bc-proof pre.code + pre.code { margin-top: .75rem; }
</style>
